BGGL -- Exterior module to linear complex
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = BGGL(P,S)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module over an exterior
        algebra
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, polynomial ring on the same
        number of vars
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, linear chain complex over S
        corresponding to P

Description
===========

Implements the left adjoint BGG functor. The more primitive function SymExt
does this only for linearly presented exterior modules.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : E = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d, SkewCommutative => true]  |
|                                                   |
|o1 = E                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = E^1/ideal(a*b,c)                          |
|                                                   |
|o2 = cokernel | ab c |                             |
|                                                   |
|                            1                      |
|o2 : E-module, quotient of E                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : betti freeResolution(P, LengthLimit => 5)     |
|                                                   |
|            0 1 2 3  4  5                          |
|o3 = total: 1 2 4 7 11 16                          |
|         0: 1 1 1 1  1  1                          |
|         1: . 1 3 6 10 15                          |
|                                                   |
|o3 : BettiTally                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hf(0..3, P)                                   |
|                                                   |
|o4 = {1, 3, 2, 0}                                  |
|                                                   |
|o4 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S = ZZ/101[x,y,z,w]                           |
|                                                   |
|o5 = S                                             |
|                                                   |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : betti BGGL(P,S)                               |
|                                                   |
|            -2 -1 0                                |
|o6 = total:  2  3 1                                |
|         0:  2  3 1                                |
|                                                   |
|o6 : BettiTally                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This script really belongs in the BGG package.

