dualWithComponents -- dual module preserving direct sum information
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = dualWithComponents M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 

Description
===========

If M is a direct sum module (isDirectSum M == true) then N is the direct sum of
the duals of the components (and this is done recursively). This SHOULD be
built into dual M, but isn't as of M2, v. 1.7

See also
========

  * *note HomWithComponents: HomWithComponents, -- computes Hom, preserving
    direct sum information
  * *note tensorWithComponents: tensorWithComponents, -- forms the tensor
    product, preserving direct sum information

Ways to use dualWithComponents:
===============================

  * "dualWithComponents(Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note dualWithComponents: dualWithComponents, is a *note method
function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

