EisenbudShamashTotal -- Precursor complex of total Ext
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (d0,d1) =  EisenbudShamashTotal M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over a complete intersection
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Check => ..., default value false
      * Grading => ..., default value 2
      * Variables => ..., default value s
  * Outputs:
      * d0, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, map of free modules over an
        enlarged ring
      * d1, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, map of free modules over an
        enlarged ring

Description
===========

Assume that M is defined over a ring of the form Rbar = R/(f_0..f_{c-1}), a
complete intersection, and that M has a finite free resolution G over R. In
this case M has a free resolution F over Rbar whose dual, F^* is a finitely
generated, Z-graded free module over a ring Sbar\cong kk[s_0..s_{c-1},gens
Rbar], where the degrees of the s_i are {-2, -degree f_i}. This resolution is
is constructed from the dual of G, together with the duals of the higher
homotopies on G defined by Eisenbud.

The function returns the differentials d0:F^*_{even} \to F^*_{odd} and
d1:F^*_{odd}\to F^*_{even}.

The maps d0,d1 form a matrix factorization of sum(c, i->s_i*f_i). The have the
property that for any Rbar module N,

HH_1 complex \{d0**N, d1**N\} = Ext^{even}_{Rbar}(M,N)

S^{{1,0}}**HH_1 complex \{S^{{-2,0}}**d1**N, d0**N\} = Ext^{odd}_{Rbar}(M,N)

This is encoded in the script newExt

Option defaults: Check=>false Variables=>getSymbol "s", Grading =>2}

If Grading =>1, then a singly graded result is returned (just forgetting the
homological grading.)



