highSyzygy -- Returns a syzygy module one beyond the regularity of Ext(M,k)
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = highSyzygy M0
  * Inputs:
      * M0, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, over a complete intersection
        ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Optimism => ..., default value 0
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a syzygy module of M0

Description
===========

A "high syzygy" over a complete intersection is one such that general
ci-operators have split kernels when applied recursively on cosyzygy chains of
previous kernels.

If p = mfBound M0, then highSyzygy M0 returns the p-th syzygy of M0. (if F is a
resolution of M this is the cokernel of F.dd_{p+1}). Optimism => r as optional
argument, highSyzygy(M0,Optimism=>r) returns the (p-r)-th syzygy. The script is
useful with matrixFactorization(ff, highSyzygy M0).

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : setRandomSeed 100                                        |
| -- setting random seed to 100                                |
|                                                              |
|o1 = 100                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ZZ/101[x,y,z]                                        |
|                                                              |
|o2 = S                                                        |
|                                                              |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = matrix"x3,y3+x3,z3+x3+y3"                            |
|                                                              |
|o3 = | x3 x3+y3 x3+y3+z3 |                                    |
|                                                              |
|             1      3                                         |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ff = f*random(source f, source f)                        |
|                                                              |
|o4 = | 10x3-22y3-4z3 -20x3-20y3-6z3 -27x3-41y3+z3 |           |
|                                                              |
|             1      3                                         |
|o4 : Matrix S  <-- S                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = S/ideal f                                            |
|                                                              |
|o5 = R                                                        |
|                                                              |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M0 = R^1/ideal"x2z2,xyz"                                 |
|                                                              |
|o6 = cokernel | x2z2 xyz |                                    |
|                                                              |
|                            1                                 |
|o6 : R-module, quotient of R                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : betti freeResolution (M0, LengthLimit => 7)              |
|                                                              |
|            0 1 2  3  4  5  6  7                              |
|o7 = total: 1 2 6 11 18 26 36 47                              |
|         0: 1 . .  .  .  .  .  .                              |
|         1: . . .  .  .  .  .  .                              |
|         2: . 1 .  .  .  .  .  .                              |
|         3: . 1 6  6  .  .  .  .                              |
|         4: . . .  5 18 14  .  .                              |
|         5: . . .  .  . 12 36 25                              |
|         6: . . .  .  .  .  . 22                              |
|                                                              |
|o7 : BettiTally                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : mfBound M0                                               |
|                                                              |
|o8 = 3                                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : M = betti freeResolution(highSyzygy M0, LengthLimit => 7)|
|                                                              |
|             0  1  2  3  4  5  6  7                           |
|o9 = total: 11 18 26 36 47 60 74 90                           |
|         6:  6  .  .  .  .  .  .  .                           |
|         7:  5 18 14  .  .  .  .  .                           |
|         8:  .  . 12 36 25  .  .  .                           |
|         9:  .  .  .  . 22 60 39  .                           |
|        10:  .  .  .  .  .  . 35 90                           |
|                                                              |
|o9 : BettiTally                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : netList BRanks matrixFactorization(ff, highSyzygy M0)   |
|                                                              |
|      +-+-+                                                   |
|o10 = |6|6|                                                   |
|      +-+-+                                                   |
|      |3|6|                                                   |
|      +-+-+                                                   |
|      |2|6|                                                   |
|      +-+-+                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

In this case as in all others we have examined, greater "Optimism" is not
justified, and thus matrixFactorization(ff, highSyzygy(M0, Optimism=>1)); would
produce an error.

Caveat
======

A bug in the total Ext script means that the oddExtModule is sometimes zero,
and this can cause a wrong value to be returned.

