makeFiniteResolutionCodim2 -- Maps associated to the finite resolution of a high syzygy module in codim 2
*********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        maps = makeFiniteResolutionCodim2(ff,mf)
  * Inputs:
      * mf, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, matrix factorization
      * ff, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, regular sequence
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Check => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * maps, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, many maps

Description
===========

Given a codim 2 matrix factorization, makes all the components of the
differential and of the homotopies that are relevant to the finite resolution,
as in 4.2.3 of Eisenbud-Peeva "Minimal Free Resolutions and Higher Matrix
Factorizations"

