makeT -- make the CI operators on a complex
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        T = makeT(ff,F,i)
        T = makeT(ff,F,t0,i)
  * Inputs:
      * ff, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 1xc matrix whose entries are
        a complete intersection in S
      * F, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, over S/ideal ff
      * t0, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, CI-operator on F for ff_0 to
        be preserved
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, define CI operators from F_i
        \to F_{i-2}
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of CI operators F_i \to F_{i-2}
        corresponding to entries of ff

Description
===========

substitute matrices of two differentials of F into S = ring ff, compose them,
and divide by entries of ff, in order. If the second Matrix argument t0 is
present, use it as the first CI operator.

The degrees of the targets of the T_j are changed by the degrees of the f_j to
make the T_j homogeneous.

