stableHom -- map from Hom(M,N) to the stable Hom module
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        p = stableHom(M,N)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * p, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, projection from Hom(M,N) to
        the stable Hom

Description
===========

The stable Hom is Hom(M,N)/T where T is the submodule of homomorphisms that
factor through a free cover of N (or, equivalently, through any projective)

See also
========

  * *note isStablyTrivial: isStablyTrivial, -- returns true if the map goes to
    0 under stableHom

Ways to use stableHom:
======================

  * "stableHom(Module,Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note stableHom: stableHom, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

